Step 1: Open Custom Agents

Go to:

Julius Custom Agents Page

Or click “Custom Agents” from the left sidebar inside Julius.

Step 2: Click “Create Agent”

Press the Create Agent button.

This opens the agent configuration screen where you define how the AI behaves.

Step 3: Give Your Agent a Name

Choose a clear descriptive name.

Examples:

Sales Dashboard Analyst
Finance Reporting Assistant
Marketing Insights Agent
SQL Data Helper

Step 4: Add Instructions

This is the most important section.

Write detailed instructions about:

What the agent should do
Tone/style
Output format
Rules it must follow

Example:

You are a financial analyst.
Always create executive summaries.
Use tables and charts when possible.
Highlight anomalies and trends.

The instructions become part of the system prompt used by Julius.

Step 5: Add Training Examples

Add sample prompts and ideal responses.

Example:

User: “Show monthly revenue trends”
Expected Output: revenue chart + business insights

This helps the agent learn your preferred workflow and response style.

Step 6: Upload Knowledge Base Files

You can connect:

CSV files
Excel sheets
PDFs
Documents
Databases

The agent will use these as its knowledge source.

Step 7: Configure Behavior

Optional settings may include:

Preferred output style
Visualization preferences
Analysis depth
Response formatting

Example:

Always generate charts
Use Python for calculations
Summarize before detailed analysis
Step 8: Save the Agent

Click Save or Create Agent.

Your custom agent is now ready.

Step 9: Activate the Agent

Open a new chat and select the agent from the agent dropdown menu.

Once activated:

Every prompt in that chat uses your agent’s configuration
The knowledge base and instructions apply automatically
Step 10: Test and Improve

Ask questions like:

“Analyze sales performance”
“Create dashboard insights”
“Forecast next quarter revenue”

Then refine:

Instructions
Training examples
Knowledge files

to improve results over time.
